        "No instrument had ever verified this pin. verify_sources.py correctly ABSTAINS on a",
        "case-insensitive filesystem ('NOT VERIFIED HERE: rlvigen needs a case-sensitive filesystem')",
        "and gate_source_reconstruction_verifies reports it as pending rather than passing -- so the",
        "pin sat unchecked, and the first machine able to check it refused it.",
        "",
        "The new value was produced by bootstrap_sources.py's own clone-and-patch path on Linux/ext4,",
        "inside a container on cds2: 1145 records. It is cross-validated against an INDEPENDENT",
        "artifact -- rlvigen-door2-90d8b8c4.tgz, the archive production has actually been running,",
        "1146 files -- and the two agree exactly but for cfgs/task/TwoArmHandOver.yaml (the",
        "case-collision pair, where the archive kept the other spelling because it too was built on",
        "macOS) and one 'results' entry the manifest excludes.",
        "",
        "So production was never running a damaged tree; only the pin and the local working copy were",
        "damaged. Do NOT regenerate this hash on macOS -- doing so silently reinstates a tree missing",
        "546 files. Recompute it only on a case-sensitive filesystem."
      ]
